  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Returnees in Eastern Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the beginning of the hostilities in Sudan on 15 April 2023, nearly 500,000 displaced individuals have fled to neighbouring Chad. Field assessments have further indicated that the most urgent needs of this population are food, shelter, non-food items (NFIs), cash and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH). 
 
Under this grant, IOM is providing Shelter/NFI and settlement support aimed towards creating a dignified sites for returnees, and vital protection during the rainy season. Additionally to address the WASH needs, this project is creating three new water access points to provide clean water for returnees, as well as the creation of latrines along with handwashing stations and the implementation of community-based hygiene promotion activities.</narrative>
  </description>
